# One index into `char: []: []: mainArgs` is an inner char Array -- a value, the Array descriptor reference (R5-3a,
# R5-G3), so comparing it with 0 is the ordinary null test of a reference.  Before: "an inner Array is a value only inside
# length()" (the two-literal-index route, gone with R5-3b).  Translation-only: the letter's arguments are the host's.
MainLetter:
    char: []: []: mainArgs
end: MainLetter

@: m MainLetter
receiveMessage: m
if: m\mainArgs[1] = 0
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 1; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
